{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I will be what I will be.</b> The One who exists perpetually in a single mode from His own essence. From this it follows that He loves existence and hates all loss and corruption opposed to existence, as it says: כִּי לֹא אֶחְפֹּץ בְּמוֹת הַמֵּת (Ezekiel 18:32). And from this it follows that He loves justice and righteousness, whose end is existence, and hates wrongdoing and cruelty, which incline toward privation and loss. On this account He hated the violence and cruelty of the Egyptians against you."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:11.515826730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}